From 6ca86622ead943b9ba9e175a46958ca441e5e08f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bwright000 <benjamin.wright.25@ucl.ac.uk>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:30:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] inkling2: fused CUDA kernels and graph changes for decode
 speed

Cuts GPU kernels per decoded token from ~7,350 to ~3,700 on Inkling 2 Mini
(RTX 5070 Ti: decode 80 -> 105 tok/s via llama-server, prefill +32-37%).

- ggml: GGML_GLU_OP_SITU (CPU + CUDA) replacing the 9-op SITU chain
- ggml: GGML_OP_INKLING_MIX fused depth attention (CPU reference + CUDA,
  split 2-kernel path for few tokens); not bit-exact, KLD at the model's
  rounding floor (~0.003, same as disabling the standard CUDA fusions)
- ggml-cuda: pattern fusions in ggml_cuda_try_fuse: L2 clip chain,
  convolve head (concat + conv-state copy) and tail (ssm_conv + residual
  + scale [+ trailing residual add]), control tanh gates, fused control
  second half (2 fp32 matvecs + gates, T<=8)
- inkling2: stacked-prefix concat cache and no query repeat at decode in
  mix(), concat-then-rms_norm in control(), strided views instead of copies
- tests: test-backend-ops cases for SITU and INKLING_MIX

TEMP A/B switches (remove before upstreaming): LLAMA_INKLING_UNFUSED,
LLAMA_INKLING_NO_MIXOP, GGML_CUDA_NO_INKLING_{CLIP,CONV,GATE,CTRL},
GGML_CUDA_INKLING_MIX_NO_SPLIT, INKLING_FUSE_DEBUG.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
